    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:a7ccc07d0e455ea2",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "04bd6e7f6eafba44606f44b07d07c8a9d1722a9a9ae9bc5e037f1804da867286",
      "text": "Day 12 · The Sacred Valley, cradle of Inca civilisation, was renowned for its fertile land and mild climate. The Incas built entire towns here, whose ruins can still be seen: Urubamba, with the country estate of the Inca emperor Huayna Cápac; Pisac, said to be shaped like a partridge; Ollantaytambo and its ceremonial centre; Chinchero, with a colonial church built on Inca foundations; and Moray, with its amphitheatre-like agricultural terraces.\n\nNear Pisac, browse the local market for handmade silver, ceramics and leather, and at the Awanakancha centre meet llamas, alpacas and vicuñas and learn how their wool is dyed. Buffet lunch at the Inka House restaurant.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1cZT1OftE-36NSMteIbFLu2h2u8tTgizH",
